[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: SPICE semiconductor profile requirements

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The full semiconductor scope includes diode, BJT and explicitly named MOS levels with model parameters, DC, AC and transient charge. This document begins the diode vertical slice; it does not close BJT/MOS or general ngspice model compatibility. Exact reuse sources and unresolved alternatives are in semiconductor-reuse-assessment.md. Parameters below are effective values at a fixed temperature; unsupported model terms refuse rather than disappear.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-DIODE-Q-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Nonlinear depletion and diffusion junction storage
STATEMENT: >>>
The bounded native SPICE diode shall evaluate physical conduction current, its voltage derivative, depletion charge integrated from CJO/VJ/M with forward continuation at FC*VJ, and diffusion charge TT*I. It shall use dQ/dV at the operating point for AC, and accepted charge differences with the matching trial derivative for backward Euler. Parameters and intermediate results outside the qualified finite domain shall reject explicitly.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/spice_diode.rs, src/model.rs, src/newton.rs, src/ac.rs, src/configured.rs. Verification: tests/spice_diode.rs and explicitly invoked tests/spice_diode_oracle.rs. Domain: effective IS>0, NVT>0, CJO>=0,VJ>0,0<=M<1,0<=FC<1,TT>=0. Temperature transformations, avalanche and series resistance remain open work. Qualification evidence pending final immutable source hashes.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-DIODE-OBS-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Explicit conduction and total current semantics
STATEMENT: >>>
A charged SPICE diode shall expose separate conduction and total terminal current observables. DC total current equals conduction; AC total current includes j*omega*dQ/dV; supported backward-Euler total current includes accepted charge differences over the accepted interval. Unsupported history or initialization semantics shall refuse instead of inventing total current. Independent KCL shall include displacement; unavailable nonlinear stored-energy verification shall report NotChecked with a reason.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/api.rs, src/audit.rs. Verification: total-current KCL and explicit unavailable-energy tests in tests/spice_diode.rs. Configured adaptive and explicitly supplied initial states are currently unsupported for this charged profile because endpoint history alone does not establish the required initial derivative or final adaptive substep current. Existing constant-capacitance diode behavior remains separately qualified.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-DIODE-BIND-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Strict model parameter binding
STATEMENT: >>>
The generated frontend shall bind qualified diode model assignments in their declaration scope with the active instance environment. It shall reject unknown, duplicate, opaque, invalid or unqualified assignments atomically before returning a request, preserve source origins, and use the same typed native model in DC, AC and transient preparation.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: dotnet/Simulator.Frontend/SemiconductorPreparation.cs, additive diode lowering in OperatingPointBridge.cs, typed DTOs in Simulator.Client/Requests.cs. Verification: SemiconductorTests.cs (8 initial cases), full frontend regressions and actual engine oracle integration. The bounded profile supports IS,N,CJO/CJ0,VJ,M,FC,TT,RS and TNOM=27. BV and other unqualified terms reject. Binding readiness is not numerical qualification.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-DIODE-AC-FLOATING-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Signed complex current of a floating charged diode
STATEMENT: >>>
The published total AC current shall use the complex differential terminal voltage V(P)-V(N), including subtraction of the imaginary part at N. With both terminals independently excited, the total device current shall equal differential voltage multiplied by the small-signal junction admittance. At each ideal source, the signed source branch current shall satisfy terminal KCL.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/api.rs. Verification: tests/spice_diode.rs::floating_diode_ac_current_uses_signed_terminal_phasor_difference, independent zero-bias Shockley slope and charge derivative on dense LU and sparse faer. Issue 41 captures the exact subtraction-to-addition mutant.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SEMI-DIODE-OBS-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-DIODE-SERIES-R-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Diode series resistance before the charged junction
STATEMENT: >>>
The frontend shall stamp positive diode model RS in ohms between the external anode and the intrinsic charged junction. Zero shall preserve the original topology. Negative values and unrepresentable conductance shall refuse. The original diode current identity shall identify the intrinsic junction current because the series branch has no additional paths.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: SemiconductorTests and compat/ngspice/tube-grid-diode.cir. The new node and resistor are subject to existing bridge resource budgets.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SEMI-DIODE-BIND-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-TUBE-12AX7-REF-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Published 12AX7 nonlinear reference comparison
STATEMENT: >>>
The simulator shall bind a pinned three-terminal 12AX7 reference subcircuit and retain its nonlinear voltage and current relations. Verification shall compare plate current over both axes of a nested DC sweep and compare common-cathode bias and complex AC gain with ngspice using the same model and circuit. A linearization supplied at a known bias shall be reported separately from nonlinear support.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Inferred from the accepted 12AX7 experiment. The published PSpice VALUE sources and their normalized nonlinear B forms remain unsupported. See evidence/grammar-cohort-checklist.md.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-BSIM330-NATIVE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Native bulk BSIM3 3.3.0 terminal currents and charges
STATEMENT: >>>
A supported four-terminal bulk BSIM3 VERSION=3.3.0 device shall evaluate signed NMOS and PMOS terminal currents and charges in the solver process. DC shall use consistent current derivatives, AC shall linearize current and charge at the operating point, and transient shall preserve accepted charge history across rejected steps. Unsupported versions, SOI model families, or unqualified parameters shall receive explicit diagnostics. The verification shall compare like model cards, geometry, temperatures and biases with ngspice and check current and charge conservation independently.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Draft inferred from the accepted model implementation request. The standalone OSDI evaluator in semiconductor-reuse-assessment.md exercises only terminal current and charge. The DC sweep and dynamic fixtures exercise the normal Rust assembly path. See the bounded provider scope and verification in semiconductor-reuse-assessment.md.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-BSIM330-DC-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Bulk BSIM3 3.3.0 DC model binding and Newton stamping
STATEMENT: >>>
The requested DC path shall bind explicit bulk LEVEL 8 or 49 VERSION 3.3.0 cards with supported model terms and SI geometry into a distinct four-terminal device. For each DC trial it shall evaluate signed D/G/S/B terminal currents in process and stamp their incremental voltage derivatives. Missing or invalid native providers and unsupported card terms shall fail explicitly.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification uses tests/bsim330.rs, the frontend MOS tests, and the independently run ngspice nested sweep. Initial provider scope is Windows x64, explicit TOX, NCH, NSUB, VTH0, W and L, optional nonnegative junction areas and perimeters, 27 Celsius, and no internal uncollapsed nodes. The native OSDI module is an opt-in external input.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SEMI-BSIM330-NATIVE-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-BSIM330-DYNAMIC-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Bulk BSIM3 3.3.0 AC and backward-Euler terminal charge
STATEMENT: >>>
At the converged bias, the AC solver shall stamp the four-terminal current Jacobian and j omega times the charge Jacobian. A backward-Euler trial shall add the difference of trial and previously accepted terminal charge divided by the step to each terminal residual, with its consistent trial derivative. Rejected trials shall leave accepted charge history unchanged. Fixed-step KCL shall include displacement current; unavailable nonlinear energy and AC physical audits shall be identified explicitly.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: tests/bsim330.rs compares ngspice gate charge, its derivative, and repeatability after a discarded trial. The BSIM3 AC, gate-ramp transient, and loaded transient fixtures in compat/ngspice are the native simulator comparisons. The model provider and parameter slice remain those of SEMI-BSIM330-DC-001.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SEMI-BSIM330-NATIVE-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-BSIM3SOI-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Distinct Berkeley BSIM3 SOI device topology and charge
STATEMENT: >>>
The simulator shall distinguish FD level 55, DD level 56, and PD level 57. It shall preserve the back gate, external body contact where present, and any internal floating-body unknown required by the selected model. Model-card parameters, dimensions, and admitted numerical settings shall retain their semantics. The same device shall contribute terminal current and charge to the requested analyses, with accepted transient history preserved on retry.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Acceptance is the 15 RSpice reference-pass decks in the pinned shared corpus. The standalone FD DC probe in scripts/Bsim3SoiFdProbe.c verifies one device sweep only. Frontend binding, Rust assembly, coupled solves, transient verification and per-deck acceptance remain open. See semiconductor-reuse-assessment.md.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-BSIM3SOI-FD-STATIC-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Pinned FD SOI static operating-point interface
STATEMENT: >>>
The typed operating-point interface shall accept the pinned Berkeley FD NMOS reference model with D/G/S/E terminal order and stamp its four signed currents and voltage derivatives. E is the back-gate terminal. An absent or invalid host shall fail explicitly. The static provider shall refuse charge-dependent analyses until terminal charge is qualified.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: tests/bsim330.rs exercises the native stamp, the normal request dispatch and the unsupported charge path. This profile is the t3 FD reference card with fixed geometry, temperature and Gmin. It does not satisfy the original deck admission or the DD/PD model requirements.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SEMI-BSIM3SOI-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-BSIM3SOI-FD-DECK-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Pinned Berkeley FD model card and original static sweeps
STATEMENT: >>>
Requested analysis preparation shall bind the pinned NMOS level-55 card with its original four terminal order and supported geometry into the FD reference device. The exact Gmin and ITL1 option profile shall apply only to circuits whose active device equations honor it. A changed model assignment, geometry, option, or unsupported dynamic request shall refuse without publishing a partial analysis.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Inferred from the RSpice device-catalog work. The model card uses lexical assignment fingerprinting, the device fixes Gmin at 1e-25 S and the bounded Newton policy uses an ITL1 limit of 500. Verification uses the original FD t3 and t5 decks, the Windows frontend negative tests, and independent ngspice DC output.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SEMI-BSIM3SOI-FD-STATIC-001
